# Generated by the regtest scripts on this machine, not part of the recipe. Each of these is
# rebuilt by chain.sh / start.sh from the tracked scripts and configs, so committing them would
# mean committing node data, a synced index, and machine-specific state that nobody can review.
regtest/data/
regtest/ord-data/
regtest/.snapshot/
regtest/.last-seen
regtest/.history
regtest/.demo/
regtest/.failbin/
regtest/bin/

# The mainnet run's own state, created by mainnet/README.md steps 1 and 2 rather than by a tracked
# script: ord-data/ is ord's index *and* its wallet, which holds the premine's keys, and
# bitcoin-data/ is the node's datadir, whose .cookie is an RPC credential. Neither can be reviewed
# in a diff, and either one staged would put a key or a password in the history permanently.
mainnet/ord-data/
mainnet/bitcoin-data/

# Backups and git bundles: large, and regenerated from the repository. A *.bundle is output, not
# a source file - it contains everything already tracked here.
*.bundle
regtest-bundle-*.tar.gz
regtest-bundle-*.tar.gz.sha256

# Working copies and vendored dependencies that are not ours to version.
threads/
loveriver/lib/

# A one-off egress measurement, not part of any recipe: a temporary TCP listener that answers one
# question - can the x10 account reach a VPS on 3306 - plus the log it writes beside itself. It was
# run once, on one machine, and opens a firewall port while it runs; it belongs to that test, not to
# the token, the regtest recipe or the mainnet run.
deploy/listen-vps-3306.ps1
deploy/listen-3306.log
